<LegalLayout locale="en" title="About Us" description="Who is behind DoctorConverter? Our approach to free, no-sign-up PDF and document tools, the open-source engines we use and how we handle your files.">
  <p><strong>DoctorConverter</strong> is a free online toolkit built to solve everyday document tasks quickly and simply. From merging PDFs to extracting text from scans, ten tools live in a single workspace, with no account required.</p>
  <h2>Why we built it</h2>
  <p>Students combine lecture notes before finals, lawyers squeeze exhibits under e-filing limits, job seekers shrink their resumes and visa applicants gather documents into one PDF. We want these jobs done in a few clicks, without ad clutter, forced sign-ups or confusing menus.</p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Conversions run on our own servers in resource-limited, isolated processes; documents are not sent to third-party processing services.</li>
    <li>We rely on proven open-source engines: QPDF, Poppler, LibreOffice, Tesseract OCR and Python document libraries.</li>
    <li>Files are reachable only from the session that uploaded them, expire automatically and can be deleted immediately.</li>
    <li>Page, size and support limits are stated in each tool’s panel; we do not pretend to do what we cannot.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>Anyone who works with documents, from students and lawyers to accountants and visa applicants. See our step-by-step <a href="/use-cases/" class="text-accent underline font-medium">use-case guides</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Ideas, bug reports or partnerships: <a href="mailto:destek@doctorconverter.com" class="text-accent underline font-medium">destek@doctorconverter.com</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
